## Touch-camera implementation

Adds a bounded input corridor to the active H-Earth public route:

- one-pointer drag emits compositor orbit intents;
- two-pointer pinch-in increases camera-distance scale and zooms out;
- two-pointer spread decreases camera-distance scale and zooms in;
- the route never owns camera state and never scales the page DOM;
- each accepted intent produces a fresh compositor handoff and incremental renderer reprojection.

The public-route path is now registered through merged prerequisite `0bcf43982f9d27ff30a1c198ca945ca0ac8a8b4b`.

A disposable workflow executes fail-closed preflight, static boundary checks, mobile touch tests, desktop pointer tests, screenshot capture, and then removes all transport files. Final intended product scope is exactly `/showroom/globe/h-earth/index.js`. User authorized implementation and promotion to `main` after executable verification.

